      "design_summary": "Wires ImageNet-1k into the ViT cell as a pure data/config change with ZERO edits to model defs, evaluate, _eval_log, train loops, or any csrc/kernel file. The harness is full-batch whole-tensor everywhere (train loops forward all of tx every step e.g. :1195; _eval_log forwards all of vax/tex :742-743; worker materializes the whole dataset on-device :1780-1786), so 1.28M ImageNet images cannot be a single tensor (~740GB). Design: (A) TRAIN returns a once-sampled, standard-augmented VIEW of train_view=8192 images from the train split (faithful to the owner budget 're-sees <1 epoch so safe'), kept full-batch so train-loop diffs stay ZERO; (B) EVAL uses ONE fixed probe of probe_n=2048 images sampled once (seed-deterministic) from the standard 50k val split with eval-transform only, cached to disk byte-identically, reused every eval (caps eval to ~1s) and returned in BOTH the val and test slots (ImageNet has one held-out set; val feeds the top-1 early-stop trigger via _eval_log's `va`, :757). The model-size coupling is applied PURELY via config keys that ViT already reads: p=1000 (out=Linear(d,p) :423; logits[:, :p] slice :539/:746), patch_dim=768=16*16*3 (patch_proj=Linear(patch_dim,d) :419), num_patches=196=(224/16)^2 (pos=Embedding(num_patches+1,d) :421) — no ViT class edit. The accuracy early-stop trigger is KEPT (top-1 from CLS); only the numeric threshold is set to a reachable 0.50 via config (not the unreachable 0.95 grokking default). Patchify is verified: unfold->permute(1,2,0,3,4)->reshape gives deterministic [196,768] row-major, C-outermost, patch0=top-left 16x16 across channels. GATING RISK flagged: the L3-TC ViT megakernel is static-pinned to the 49/16/97/32-tensor/418017-param layout (INTEGRATION-VIT.md; vit_layout.cuh static_asserts), so an ImageNet-shaped ViT HARD-RAISES inside _try_fused_train_step (:794, no silent fallback) until a sibling codegens a new vit_imagenet cell — a separate kernel task, out of scope for this data wiring. Transport-only: no kernel math, GEMM order, or ascending-k fp32 reduction touched, so the fp64/SAM numerics gate and A/A/A determinism for existing cells are unaffected; gfx942/tpu_v6e untouched.",
