      "design_summary": "The kernel side already exists: csrc/backends/cuda/sm_90/primitives.cuh:387 defines L2PersistScope (RAII over cudaStreamSetAttribute + cudaAccessPolicyWindow + cudaDeviceSetLimit(cudaLimitPersistingL2CacheSize,...), gated ENABLE_L2_PERSIST at :383), but a grep of csrc/ + grokking_optimizers/ shows it is instantiated NOWHERE — only the class body and the doc-comment example. So the two missing pieces are exactly (a) a compile.py tuned dim and (b) wiring it into the launch. I add three generic, config-declared dims to _sm90_full_space() (compile.py:2122) after pipe_depth (2293-2294): l2_persist (bool, SG_TUNED_L2_PERSIST, default False), l2_hit_ratio (float, SG_TUNED_L2_HIT_RATIO, default 1.0 == the hardcoded hitRatio at primitives.cuh:429), and l2_setaside_pct (int percent-of-max, SG_TUNED_L2_SETASIDE_PCT, default 100 == the full-span SetLimit at primitives.cuh:424) — first value reproduces today's behaviour so the canonical build is byte-identical; all applies_to=[\"device\"] and sm_90-only, so HIP/TPU spaces are untouched. The single non-obvious wiring point is _tc_relevant_device_flags (compile.py:14888) — an explicit allowlist (keep_macros, 14897-14900) that DROPS every device -D except tile/split-K before the real-TC TU build, so the new macros must be added there or they never reach the megakernel; the dim names also go into _GEMM_TILE_DIM_NAMES (14840) so a config varying them is timed on the real TC step (the cheap opt.step timer is blind to a launch-time stream attribute). resolve_macros (3299-3308) needs a float branch because l2_hit_ratio is the project's first float-valued macro (_format_value at 3266-3273 emits str(float) with no 'f' suffix — a benign double literal; the branch emits a clean float literal). On the kernel side primitives.cuh gains three #ifndef SG_TUNED_L2_* default #defines (so the _kernel_source_macros scanner marks the dims live and they auto-activate) and the ctor reads the tuned hitRatio + a percent-of-max set-aside (clamped to [span, max_persist]); fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh wraps the persistent launch (1561-1568) in an #if SG_TUNED_L2_PERSIST RAII block constructing L2PersistScope over st.exp_avg|st.exp_avg_sq, which the launcher (mega_decoder_real_adamw_tc_launcher.cu:138-143) binds as a contiguous 2*kDecTotalElems float block. The change is hint-only (L2 residency cannot alter the ascending-k fp32 order or any value), so it is a transport-only legal rewrite; default OFF makes the canonical config a literal no-op, keep/revert-ratchet safe, with the perf win + A/A/A re-run silicon-gated.",
