      "area": "S1.5 smem carveout dim (cudaFuncAttributePreferredSharedMemoryCarveout + tuned MaxDynamicSharedMemorySize)",
      "design_summary": "The autotuner reaches kernels through only two channels: `-DSG_TUNED_*` macros via resolve_macros (compile.py:3276-3309) and bare ptxas flags via resolve_extra_nvcc_flags (compile.py:3312-3409). There is no runtime channel into the launch wrappers, so the only generic way to make the carveout + max-dyn-smem launch attributes tunable is to have the launchers READ two new `SG_TUNED_*` macros — the same idiom as SG_TUNED_MEGA_BLOCK/SG_TUNED_TILE_N. This auto-marks the dims LIVE via the source scanner _kernel_source_macros (compile.py:1348-1378) used by _is_dead_dim (1546-1577), and keeps config_key distinct via _dead_key_dims (1626-1658) — no edits to those derivations needed. Today every megakernel launcher already calls cudaFuncSetAttribute(MaxDynamicSharedMemorySize, ...) with a FIXED sizeof: decoder fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh:1531-1536 (sizeof(DecTcSmem) under SG_DEC_TC_DYNAMIC_SMEM, else 0 at :1538), vit :309-316 (sizeof(VitSampleSmem)), mamba :1250-1253 + helper :1222-1224 (kMambaSmemBytes). compile.py never sweeps that value. PreferredSharedMemoryCarveout is set nowhere (grep over csrc/+grokking_optimizers/ finds only the unrelated CUTLASS StageCountAutoCarveout in mma.cuh). The draft adds two _dim() entries in _sm90_full_space (compile.py inserted after grad_tile at :2188): smem_carveout [-1,100,0,25,50,75]->SG_TUNED_SMEM_CARVEOUT and max_dyn_smem_kb [0,100,164,200,228]->SG_TUNED_MAX_DYN_SMEM_KB, both applies_to=['device']. First value of each is the OMIT/EXACT sentinel (-1 skips the carveout call; 0 opts into exactly sizeof) so the canonical build calls the same CUDA APIs with the same arguments as today (byte-/behavior-identical, revert-safe). Launchers compute opt_in = clamp(max(req, KB*1024), cudaDevAttrMaxSharedMemoryPerBlockOptin) but keep the <<<>>> dynamic-byte arg and the occupancy cert at the REAL req — so the >=1-CTA/SM hang-freedom guard and all kernel accesses are unchanged, making it parity-clean (no math, no fp32 order, HARD fp64/SAM gate untouched). Portability: carveout is CUDA-only (no hipFuncAttributePreferredSharedMemoryCarveout exists; platform.h:215-227 aliases only the max-dyn-smem attr), guarded with #if GROK_CUDA; max-dyn-smem flows through the existing gpu* alias; Pallas/tpu_v6e never see device macros. Verified: all three TUs #include csrc/fused/megakernel_common.cuh (decoder:44, vit:50, mamba:55) so the two #ifndef defaults hoist there, and cudaDevAttrMaxSharedMemoryPerBlockOptin is already used at wgmma_selftest.cu:273.",
      "draft_path": "/workspace/phase2/s15_smem_carveout.md",
      "files_to_change": [
        "csrc/fused/megakernel_common.cuh — add two #ifndef SG_TUNED_SMEM_CARVEOUT (-1) / SG_TUNED_MAX_DYN_SMEM_KB (0) default guards (PREFERRED single location; all three TUs include it at decoder:44/vit:50/mamba:55)",
        "csrc/fused/sm_90/fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh:1531-1545 — replace dyn-smem opt-in/cert region with opt_in ceiling (clamped to cudaDevAttrMaxSharedMemoryPerBlockOptin) + #if GROK_CUDA carveout cudaFuncSetAttribute; <<<>>> arg at :1566 and occ query unchanged",
        "csrc/fused/sm_90/fused_vit_megakernel.cuh:309-322 — same opt_in/carveout block; <<<>>> at :343 + occ query :320-322 unchanged",
        "csrc/fused/sm_90/fused_mamba_megakernel.cuh:1250-1258 and helper mb_tc_launched_nctas:1222-1227 — same opt_in clamp (helper: no carveout, does not launch)",
        "grokking_optimizers/compile.py:2188 (insert after grad_tile, before the L3-TC tile dims block) — add _dim('smem_carveout','int',[-1,100,0,25,50,75],'SG_TUNED_SMEM_CARVEOUT',['device']) and _dim('max_dyn_smem_kb','int',[0,100,164,200,228],'SG_TUNED_MAX_DYN_SMEM_KB',['device'])",
        "grokking_optimizers/compile.py:1300-1303 — add 'smem_carveout','max_dyn_smem_kb' to _LIVE_TUNING_DIMS (optional defensive floor for the no-source-tree case)",
        "grokking_optimizers/compile.py:2296-2325 — add prefilter rules carveout_range and max_dyn_smem_fits (optional guard mirroring the runtime clamp)"
      ],
      "risks": [
        "max_dyn_smem_kb is the higher-value but riskier knob: a too-large ceiling can interact with the >=1-CTA/SM occupancy cert. Mitigated because the cert re-queries with the REAL req (not the inflated ceiling) and the existing `if(occ<1) return cudaErrorLaunchOutOfResources` drops the variant; still flagged NEEDS-PARITY before a non-default winner ships. If the tournament wants the absolute-minimal S1.5, ship ONLY the carveout dim (pure hint, parity-trivial).",
        "On ViT (~184KB) and Mamba (~227KB) the required dyn-smem already sits near the 228KB cap, so max_dyn_smem_kb clamps to the device cap and is effectively pinned there — the dim only sweeps freely on the decoder (17.6-49.6KB footprint). This asymmetry is fine but means the ceiling lever is decoder-only in practice.",
        "Carveout is CUDA-only; on HIP (gfx942) the macro is read inside an #if GROK_CUDA block so it is inert. The scanner still sees the token in csrc/, so the dim is marked LIVE on HIP too and could waste trial budget unless the per-arch space pins it — the draft keeps applies_to=['device'] and relies on the carveout being a no-op; lead may want an explicit HIP pin so the HIP autotuner does not sweep a behavior-identical knob.",
        "Parity claim (no math change) rests on the <<<>>> dynamic-byte arg and every kernel access staying at the exact required bytes while only the func-attribute ceiling widens — must be confirmed by nvcc -E at default macros plus the HARD fp64(1e-4)/SAM(2.5e-2)+A/A/A gate at any non-default winner.",
        "Carveout value is a HINT the driver rounds/clamps; on SKUs where the kernel already requests near-full dynamic smem the driver is forced to MaxShared regardless, so the carveout sweep may show near-zero signal there — expected, not a correctness risk, but tuning yield is SKU-dependent."
      ]
    },
