      "name": "p2_s34_negcache_bugs",
      "phase": "P2",
      "area": "S3.4 negative cache + bloom dedup, and three compile.py/dispatch.py bug fixes",
      "design_summary": "Read the real code (compile.py 32900 lines, dispatch.py 2013, bindings.cpp 296). PART A (S3.4): infeasible/fail/numerical_fail/cost_model_pruned configs are recorded only WITHIN a run today (run_bayesian sets rec[\"status\"]=\"infeasible\" at compile.py:6631, \"fail\" at 6644, cost_model_pruned at 6660; numerical_fail at 16546/16556) — none persist across runs as a hard skip, and the exhaustive sweep re-streams the full Cartesian every run (iter_prefilter at 16346). I designed a per-(opt,model,arch) \"negcache\" sub-dict on the existing CompileCache entry (rides the v4 save/merge/lock cycle, no version bump) holding a pure-Python base64-serialised bloom filter (_NegCacheBloom: 2^21 bits, k=13, double-hashing over one sha256, no struct/deps) plus a bounded exact \"reasons\" dict for collision-free confirm, invalidated whenever hash_space(space,arch) changes. Config identity reuses the existing config_key() (compile.py:3468, already dead-dim-excluding) so the negcache dedups on the same identity as variant_artifacts. Gate points: run_bayesian gains negcache_probe/negcache_sink closures (kept CompileCache-free for its self-test callers) skipping before timer(cfg); _run_exhaustive skips before result=timer(cfg) at 16530 and harvests fail/numerical_fail at 16536-16551; both already have cache+space_hash in scope (16447/16451/16503). Safety: it ONLY skips work, never injects a winner or relaxes the fp64/SAM/A-A-A gate (pick_winner at 16578 untouched); seen() requires bloom-hit AND exact confirm so a collision never skips a never-seen config; gated behind a new BuildSpec.enable_negcache so the determinism lane runs it OFF (byte-identical no-skip path) and ON (reproducible skips). PART B bugs: (1) compile.py:17652 import is NOT a ModuleNotFoundError no-op as the task stated — I empirically proved it resolves via the self-referential sys.modules alias registered at 32885, so run_device_pgo_round (defined in-module at 32288) DOES run; the real defect is the fragile alias-dependent import + swallowed except ImportError, fixed by calling the in-module function directly. (2) resolve_extra_hipcc_flags (3424-3427) emits -amdgpu-max-num-vgprs=-1 for the _MAXRREGCOUNT_UNCAPPED (-1) sentinel that the NVCC sibling skips at 3355; the value list prepends -1 as the canonical first build (1734) so the canonical gfx942 config ships a malformed flag — fixed by mirroring the `int(v) != _MAXRREGCOUNT_UNCAPPED` guard (gfx942-only, removal-only). (3) GROK_ABI_SCHEMA is exported (bindings.cpp:120/153) but bindings.cpp:116 explicitly owes the Python assert to dispatch.py and none exists — added EXPECTED_ABI_SCHEMA=1 and an assertion in _LazyOps._resolve() (dispatch.py:478) that hard-fails on a present-mismatch (UnsupportedArchError, \"fail loudly\" per the C++ comment) and warns-then-proceeds on an absent attr, with __bool__ (521) swallowing the raise so has_kernels() stays a clean predicate.",
      "draft_path": "/workspace/phase2/s34_and_bugs.md",
      "files_to_change": [
        "grokking_optimizers/compile.py:17650-17666 (bug1: drop alias import + bare except, call in-module run_device_pgo_round)",
        "grokking_optimizers/compile.py:3417-3420 + 3422-3427 (bug2: docstring + add `int(v) != _MAXRREGCOUNT_UNCAPPED` HIPCC sentinel guard)",
        "grokking_optimizers/dispatch.py:~460 (add EXPECTED_ABI_SCHEMA=1)",
        "grokking_optimizers/dispatch.py:478-492 (bug3: ABI-schema assertion in _LazyOps._resolve)",
        "grokking_optimizers/dispatch.py:521-522 (bug3: __bool__ swallows UnsupportedArchError)",
        "grokking_optimizers/compile.py:~32280 (add _NegCacheBloom class + _negcache_config_hash helper, before run_device_pgo_round@32288)",
        "grokking_optimizers/compile.py:7346-7391 + 8036-8040 (add negcache default to _fresh_entry + get() defaulting)",
        "grokking_optimizers/compile.py:~8154 (CompileCache: _negcache_entry/negcache_seen/negcache_add + _NEGCACHE_REASONS_CAP)",
        "grokking_optimizers/compile.py:7957-8011 (_merge_disk_entries: negcache union-merge block)",
        "grokking_optimizers/compile.py:6488-6505 + 6624-6636 + 6631/6644/6660 (run_bayesian: signature + gate + harvest)",
        "grokking_optimizers/compile.py:16451-16454 + 16884-16886 (_run_bayesian: pass closures + numerical_fail harvest)",
        "grokking_optimizers/compile.py:16525-16551 (_run_exhaustive: negcache skip before timer@16530 + fail/numerical harvest)",
        "grokking_optimizers/compile.py:8488 (BuildSpec: add enable_negcache: bool = True)",
        "grokking_optimizers/compile.py:21768 (_self_test_cache: +4 negcache cases) + 23134 (_self_test_flags: +1 gfx942 sentinel case) + 26861 (bump _SELF_TEST_EXPECTED_COUNT, currently 265)"
      ],
      "risks": [
        "BUG#1 PREMISE CORRECTION (verified empirically): the compile.py:17652 import is NOT a ModuleNotFoundError no-op — it resolves via the self-referential sys.modules alias at 32885 and the device-PGO round DOES execute. The fix is a robustness/clarity cleanup (remove fragile alias-dependent import + swallowed ImportError), not a 'PGO was never running' fix. Lead must confirm he wants the inline cleanup vs leaving the working-but-fragile import.",
        "BUG#3 behaviour change: a genuinely-mismatched prebuilt .so today loads and mis-marshals silently; after the fix it raises UnsupportedArchError on first kernel use (the intended 'fail loudly' per bindings.cpp:108-119). __bool__ swallow keeps has_kernels() False rather than raising. Confirm no caller relies on a mismatched .so limping along.",
        "Negcache flaky-build masking: a config that fails to compile once due to a transient toolchain hiccup could be cached as 'fail' forever for that space_hash. RECOMMEND caching ONLY deterministic classes (prefilter-infeasible + numerical_fail + cost_model_pruned) and NOT transient build/time 'fail'; the draft currently caches 'fail' too — lead chooses. Leaning to dropping the 'fail' harvest.",
        "Bloom false-positive: mitigated by requiring bloom-hit AND exact reasons-dict confirm in negcache_seen; a reasons-evicted-but-bloom-set entry returns False (re-evaluates) so eviction can only cost time, never correctness. CPython-3.11 dict insertion order assumed for FIFO eviction (env is 3.11).",
        "Determinism/A-A-A: a fresh cache makes ZERO skips so the run is byte-identical to today; feature gated behind enable_negcache so the determinism lane can prove both the OFF (no-skip) and ON (reproducible-skip) paths. space_hash must be the exact value already threaded (hash_space@3458) — do not recompute.",
        "Self-test count_guard (compile.py:26927) enforces _SELF_TEST_EXPECTED_COUNT==265; every added _run() case must bump it in the SAME commit (e.g. 265 -> 270 for 1 flag + 4 cache cases).",
        "Keep/revert ratchet: land bug1/bug2/bug3/negcache as SEPARATE commits (bug2/bug3 safest, negcache largest surface) so the ratchet can bisect independently. bindings.cpp is intentionally NOT changed (no forced ABI rebuild)."
      ]
