      "area": "Per-function silicon verification harness (sm_90 / L3-TC): isolation + ablation/wiring matrix over the Python dispatch path and the device functions reachable via _ops, driven 8-GPU-wide, reusing the existing fp64+A/A/A gates.",
      "design_summary": "The harness is a driver layer over the EXISTING gates, not a new oracle. ISOLATION reuses run_cell_gate (tests/hw/test_l3tc_tail_gate.py:1062) whose (1a) params-vs-fp64 (gate:1349), (1b) STATE-vs-fp64 (gate:1383), (1b-sam) sam_dir-vs-pure-fp64, and (2) A/A/A determinism (gate:1409-1411) already isolate every apply_optimizer<Opt> arm (opt_components.cuh:381, enum :53), every staged precompute (opt_stages_precompute.cuh optimizer_precompute_stage<OptId> :637), the SAM 2nd backward, and SG2 (run_sg2_gate); the SG family routes to _run_sg_cell_gate (gate:682). I enumerate the sm_90 surface from the real trace fused_train_step (dispatch.py:1512) -> ops.fused_step (bindings.cpp:164) -> sg::fused_step (dispatch.cpp:632) -> mega_*_real_adamw_tc_launcher.cu -> fused_<model>_megakernel<Opt> -> per-phase device fns (dectc_/vittc_/mbtc_ forward/backward/gemm/dw/attn/ln families in model_stage_*_tc.cuh; the P2 ascending-CTA reduce; apply_scalars; sg2_stage_* in opt_stage_supergrok2.cuh). The NEW teeth are the ablation half: a default-OFF -DSG_ABLATE=<bitmask> compile-time seam (mirroring the existing SG_TUNED_GEMM_IMPL macro, fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh:86) that no-ops one phase, rebuilt as a separately-named shadow _ops via the existing tuning/decoder_bench.py build_variant + ninja/sccache machinery (scripts/fast_triage.py). The predicate: a load-bearing phase, when ablated, must FLIP the gate control-PASS->ablated-FAIL vs the SG_ABLATE=0 control build; no change => dead/unwired => FLAG. Each ablation has a documented witness cell whose failure signature the gate already records (e.g. grokfast cold-start ema ~50x off gate:1358, grokadamw global-beta1 m-rel ~0.895 gate:341, looksam sam_dir~0 gate:1222). Edge coverage is a seed sweep {42,7,123,999} that exercises the clip-fires branch (gate cites GATE_SEED=7) plus multistep witnesses for step-1-inert mechanisms. 8-GPU driving reuses the gate's own subprocess-per-cell isolation (_run_cell_gate_subprocess gate:1433) pooled across CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES via the concurrent.futures pattern verify_all already uses; subprocess boundary is required because detect_arch/_ops import is lru_cached per-process (dispatch.py:266, dispatch.cpp:147). gfx942/tpu are preserved: the macro lands only in sm_90 headers (#ifndef default keeps the .hip tree compiling), the runner is arch==90-gated and falls back to the existing gfx942 verify_all phase-3 + check_math_single_source for AMD, and TPU is rejected at the C++ boundary (dispatch.cpp:39).",
