        "NEW tests/hw/phase4_ablation_matrix.py (ABLATE registry: phase bit -> witness cell + predicted observable, Section 4.3)"
      ],
      "risks": [
        "Ablation predicate inherits the gate's blind spots: single-step run_cell_gate is BLIND to step-1-inert mechanisms (grad-clip, prodigy-d, SG2 CSA fidelity; documented gate:341/371/528). Mitigation: drive the multistep witnesses (_multistep_grokadamw_parity / _prodigy_multistep_parity / --sg11-warmup) for exactly those ablations, listed per-row.",
        "The SG_ABLATE=0 control build must be byte-A/A/A-identical to production _ops; if the macro insertion perturbs codegen the whole ablation set is void. The harness's first assertion is control==production A/A/A.",
        "Leaf GEMM/dW helpers (dectc_gemm_fwd, *_dw_run_tile, *_attn_*_tile) are too fine for a runtime ablation macro; they get only phase-level ablation + a static cuobjdump SASS-presence hand-off to Phase 5. No 'every leaf silicon-ablated' claim is made.",
        "~12 cross-file one-line edits in the megakernel headers must be mechanically mirrored across decoder/vit/mamba; a missed mirror on one model leaves that model's phase un-ablatable (caught because its witness cell would show no flip -> FLAG, but it would mis-attribute as dead-code).",
        "mamba SAM/SG ablations re-exercise the shared mamba forward whose A/A/A spill was only recently fixed (gate:387); an ablation build that changes register pressure could re-trip the spill and produce a FALSE ablation-FAIL unattributable to the removed phase. Pin __noinline__ + diff vs the SG_ABLATE=0 mamba control.",
        "Shadow-build storage/time: ~12 ablation tokens each ninja-incremental but a cold sccache makes the first build of each token slow; serialize builds, parallelize only the gate RUNS across the 8 GPUs."
      ]
